      "title": "New Migration",
      "description": "### we need to add a new migration to update our database with the new Data Model changes : \n\n>> dotnet ef migrations add AddLastUpdatedBy --output-dir Data/Migrations"
    },
    {
      "file": "Notes/00-Authentication/Lesson02.09/src/GameStore.Api/Features/Games/CreateGame/CreateGameEndpoint.cs",
      "description": "the default JWT handler remaps sub to ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier (http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/nameidentifier). After mapping, sub isn’t present, so FindFirstValue(JwtRegisteredClaimNames.Sub) returns null.\n\n\n- We need .Net to use the Sub Claim insted ",
      "line": 31,
      "title": "Bug"
    },
    {
      "file": "Notes/00-Authentication/Lesson02.09/src/GameStore.Api/Program.cs",
      "description": "AddAuthentication().AddJwtBearer(options => options.MapInboundClaims = false; ) \nkeeps inbound JWT claims un-mapped, so standard names like sub, aud, iss remain exactly as in the token. This lets you read user.\n\nFindFirstValue(JwtRegisteredClaimNames.Sub) without .NET converting it to ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier. \nEnsure the auth middleware (app.UseAuthentication(); app.UseAuthorization();) runs so tokens are actually validated and claims populated.",
      "line": 34,
      "title": "Solution"
    },
    {
